{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Fill your hands.</b> ילויני\"ש בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>Soot of the furnace.</b> A thing blown from coals thoroughly burned in the furnace; and in לַעַז אולבי\"ש." "<b>Soot.</b> A term of הֲפָחָה — the wind blows it and scatters it." "<b>And Moshe threw.</b> And anything thrown with force is thrown only with one hand — here are many miracles: one, that the handful of Moshe held enough to fill both his and Aharon's hands; and one, that the dust spread over all the land of Egypt (Tanchuma)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French emplenis, 'fill up'", 1 "the la'az is Old French souillage, 'soot/grime'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:12.579426059Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}